# Uninitialised read in IdShimmerTrans (id_sys.cpp, the heat-shimmer quad of the 2D screen
# units: the WARNING screen's text, title and menu units with trans_type shimmer): the depth
# `dot` that scales the indirect warp is read from indMtx before indMtx is written (the
# effect version, esp_sub.cpp, takes the effect's real depth along the camera). What the
# stack held there differs between builds: the compare run 32/64 bit of 18.10.2026 had frame
# 301 (WARNING) different only where such a warp acts (the edges of the text, faint waves
# around it; max 35 of 255, same GX counts), every compared frame of r120 and r100 identical
# (the next compare run confirms the cause). indMtx now starts at zero: dot 0 -> 1500 (the
# clamp), the strongest warp, on every build alike.
--- a/src/game/id_sys.cpp
+++ b/src/game/id_sys.cpp
@@ -1333,7 +1333,10 @@
     GXSetIndTexOrder(0, 1, 0);
     GXSetIndTexCoordScale(0, 0, 0);
     {
-        f32 indMtx[2][3];
+        // PORT: the depth below reads indMtx before anything is stored in it (in the original as
+        // well, what the GameCube found there is not known): zeros give dot = 0, clamped to 1500,
+        // the strongest warp, the same on every build (patch 0083)
+        f32 indMtx[2][3] = {};
         Vec d3;
         Vec d2;
         d2.x = ((Vec*) indMtx)->x;
